        "original_id": "d2eefe07-d770-5efb-befb-f6936dc41995",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Get Over It, That '70s Show, But I'm a Cheerleader, Shrink, A Midsummer Night's Dream\n- People: Mila Kunis, Ben Foster, Kirsten Dunst, Melissa Sagemiller, Sisqó, Shane West, Colin Hanks, Zoe Saldana, Swoosie Kurtz, Ed Begley Jr., Carmen Electra, Martin Short, William Shakespeare\n- Companies: Ignite Entertainment\n- Topics: film releases, casting, acting careers, adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Get Over It is a 2001 American teen comedy film loosely based on William Shakespeare's A Midsummer Night's Dream.\n- Get Over It follows a high school senior who tries to win back his ex-girlfriend by joining the school play in which she and her new boyfriend are performing, despite his friends' advice.\n- Get Over It was released on March 9, 2001.\n- Get Over It stars Ben Foster, Kirsten Dunst, Melissa Sagemiller, Sisqó, Shane West, Colin Hanks, Zoe Saldana, Mila Kunis, Swoosie Kurtz, Ed Begley Jr., Carmen Electra, and Martin Short.\n- Ignite Entertainment's films include But I'm a Cheerleader (1999), Get Over It (2001), and Shrink (2009).\n- Mila Kunis was born on August 14, 1983, and is an American actress.\n- Before age 15, Mila Kunis appeared in several television series and commercials and then gained her first significant role as Jackie Burkhart on That '70s Show.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
